#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115231 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115062} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048678} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050825}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115492} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115493} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265922} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299608} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299609} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299610} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299614} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338990} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338992} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354631} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604616} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604622}] :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115232 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115063} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115732} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115977} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256747} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265923} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265924} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265925} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292874} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299615} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299617} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299618} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299619} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604586} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604610}] :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115233 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115064} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115733} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115740} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265926} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265927} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299621} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299622} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299623} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299624} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403495} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604576} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604609}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116490 :tutorial/content "Matrices can be used to represent systems of equations, such as the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=5 \\\\ 4x\\text{ }-\\text{ }5y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\times 2$ system like the one above, we put the coefficients of the system into a $2\\times 2$ matrix, called the **coefficient matrix**:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{2}} & {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{4}} & {\\color{red}{-5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nEach row has the coefficients of one of the equations in the system, and each column consists of the coefficients of one particular variable.\nWe also have the $2\\times 1$ column vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{blue}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{blue}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n\\mathbf{x}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{b}$ consists of each constant on the right side of the system and $\\mathbf{x}$ contains the variables.\nWith these matrices, we can write our system as $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ or\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{2}} & {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{4}} & {\\color{red}{-5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{blue}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{blue}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe can write any system of two equations with two variables in this form.\nJust to check that the above equation is true, let's multiply out the left-hand side to see if it equals the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x+3y \\\\ 4x\\text{ }-\\text{ }5y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =b\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "d49da49a-c3f8-5718-91a9-4adc236155d2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3048 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
